1. Password security — sabse important
Abhi signup mein password plain text mein save ho raha hai aur login mein direct comparison ho raha hai.

Password ko bcrypt ya argon2 se hash karo. Plain-text passwords database mein store nahi karne chahiye.

3. Cookie settings
Tum secure: true use kar rahe ho. Local development mein plain HTTP par cookie set nahi hogi. Development aur production ke liye cookie settings alag rakho. httpOnly: true achha security measure hai.

4. Error handling
Tum routes mein try/catch use kar rahe ho, jo useful hai. Agla step centralized error middleware banana hai taake error responses ek jagah manage ho sakein.

Professional readiness check karne ke liye ab ye verify karo ke tum:
- Apna code bina tutorial copy kiye samjha aur modify kar sakte ho.
- Authentication aur authorization ka difference explain kar sakte ho.
- Validation, password hashing aur error handling sahi implement kar sakte ho.
- Project ko deploy karke real requests test kar sakte ho

Ab PERN developer banne ke liye kya karna hai?
1. Node.js fundamentals — modules, async/await, events, environment variables.
2. PostgreSQL practice — CRUD, relationships, joins, constraints aur queries.
3. React + Express + PostgreSQL connect karo — frontend se API call karke database ka data dikhao.
4. Authentication — signup, login, password hashing, JWT/cookies aur authorization.
5. Ek complete project banao — jaise e-commerce app, admin dashboard ya task manager.